+### Type-check locally
+
+Type-check locally before deploying when you can. A deploy compiles the app and
+reports build errors, but it does not type-check. Framework releases are
+published to npm as `apps` under the `beta` tag. The `latest` tag and the
+`1.0.0-beta` versions are unrelated packages, so install only the exact version
+pinned in `package.json`, never `apps@latest` or an unpinned `apps`.
+
+A host can run its own build of the framework that npm does not have, such as a
+version with a `-basalt.` suffix. Check first: `npm view` prints the version
+only when npm has it. The chain below stops before installing when it does not:
 
 ```sh
 cd hello
-npm install --no-package-lock
-npx -y -p typescript@7 tsc --ignoreConfig --noEmit --strict --skipLibCheck \
-  --module nodenext --moduleResolution nodenext --target es2022 index.ts
+version="$(node -p 'require("./package.json").dependencies.apps')" &&
+  [ -n "$(npm view "apps@$version" version 2>/dev/null)" ] &&
+  npm install --no-package-lock &&
+  npx -y -p typescript@7 tsc --ignoreConfig --noEmit --strict --skipLibCheck \
+    --module nodenext --moduleResolution nodenext --target es2022 index.ts
 ```
 
